& [Purpose]
  + compile one exact supplied scope and one or two lightweight LookaheadStitch declarations into deterministic lifecycle and invocation-projection records without calling a model or mutating a prompt
  + retain enough public data to prove that active stitches remain present through every covered stop tool-result resume and reentry coordinate and leave projection only through an exact fulfilled invalidated released or replacement event

& [ProfilesAndBounds]
  + [LAS-001] request profile is cantor-sjs-compiled-lookahead-stitch-request/0.1 envelope profile is cantor-sjs-compiled-lookahead-stitch-envelope/0.1 verification profile is cantor-sjs-compiled-lookahead-stitch-verification/0.1 and evidence profile is cantor-sjs-compiled-lookahead-stitch-evidence/0.1
  + [LAS-002] strict compact UTF-8 canonical JSON refuses unknown duplicate noncanonical and trailing content and is bounded to request bytes 1048576 evidence bytes 8388608 depth 40 fields 16384 and ordinary text 4096
  + [LAS-003] stitches are 1 through 2 key hints 1 through 8 per stitch source bindings 1 through 8 per stitch completion cues exactly 1 invalidators 1 through 8 observations 1 through 64 invocation coordinates 1 through 32 and projected bytes at most 8192 with checked arithmetic
  + [LAS-004] input class is exactly synthetic_provider_free_fixture or supplied_unobserved_declaration and the retained fixture cannot be relabeled as supplied unobserved

& [ScopeAndDeclaration]
  + [LAS-005] request binds distinct nonnil lowercase UUID-bearing request run scope packet and policy identities exact source snapshots input class nonauthority evidence references observation sequence and self-excluding request digest
  + [LAS-006] ExactScope binds objective phase feature requirement artifact inclusive invocation interval declared model provider tool-policy and authority-ceiling identities completion conditions invalidation conditions and scope digest
  + [LAS-007] each LookaheadStitchDeclaration binds distinct identity optional predecessor identity SubjectAnchor SemanticTurn Transform exact scope identity ordered unique KeyHints ordered unique SourceBindings one CompletionCue ordered unique Invalidators and self-excluding declaration digest
  + [LAS-008] SemanticTurn kind is exactly select_distinction conserve_invariant expose_relationship change_abstraction_level introduce_counterexample or route_evidence_gate and its description is exact supplied public text
  + [LAS-009] SourceBinding class is exactly governing_anchor plan_hint observed_coordinate or nonauthority_evidence; only governing_anchor may carry imported authority and no other class is promoted by compilation
  + [LAS-010] CompletionCue and Invalidator predicates use exact typed equality over supplied public observation fields; P0 performs no embedding confidence synonym probabilistic or model-mediated matching

& [CompilationAndLifecycle]
  + [LAS-011] compilation verifies exact scope source and authority correspondence orders stitches by identity preserves caller order only for KeyHints and emits immutable packet and projection-template digests
  + [LAS-012] lifecycle states are exactly proposed active fulfilled invalidated and released; every declaration starts proposed and activation requires exact source bindings scope identity and absence of a matching invalidator
  + [LAS-013] proposed may become active; active may become fulfilled invalidated or released; no other transition is admitted and terminal states never reactivate
  + [LAS-014] replacement requires a new stitch identity whose predecessor names one terminal stitch and whose complete declaration is independently digested; silent active mutation and identity reuse fail closed
  + [LAS-015] exact completion observation moves active to fulfilled exact invalidator observation moves proposed or active to invalidated and exact scope-exit observation moves active to released with invalidator precedence over completion and completion over scope exit
  + [LAS-016] every admitted or refused transition emits an immutable LifecycleReceipt with ordinal observation identity before and after state disposition reason packet digest and self-excluding receipt digest

& [ProjectionAndContinuity]
  + [LAS-017] an InvocationCoordinate binds exact invocation ordinal phase objective feature requirement artifact model provider tool policy authority ceiling boundary kind and last accepted receipt identity
  + [LAS-018] boundary kind is exactly initial resume_after_stop resume_after_tool_result or reentry; every coordinate inside scope with matching identities receives every active stitch exactly once in lexicographic stitch order
  + [LAS-019] a ProjectionRecord binds coordinate digest packet digest active stitch identities compact rendered stitch bytes total projected bytes and self-excluding projection digest
  + [LAS-020] rendered stitch data contains identity SubjectAnchor SemanticTurn Transform Scope KeyHints SourceBindings CompletionCue and Invalidators; it never copies source bodies proofs transcripts private reasoning or unrelated context
  + [LAS-021] a mismatch in scope source model provider tool policy authority ceiling invocation interval or packet digest emits typed refusal and no partial projection
  + [LAS-022] lifecycle and projection are evaluated in exact observation order; equal inputs produce byte-identical packet receipts projections verification and evidence manifest
  + [LAS-023] the compiler emits data only; ever-present means an authorized future host can reintroduce a verified active projection record at each covered invocation and does not mean fixed attention weight hidden state K/V cache or neuron persistence

& [VerificationAndFailure]
  + [LAS-024] request scope declaration packet observation coordinate receipt projection envelope and evidence digests are domain-separated deterministic and self-excluding; normalization applies only to fields declared sets
  + [LAS-025] independent verification reparses retained request bytes recompiles twice byte-compares packet lifecycle receipts projection records envelope verification and reconstructed evidence manifest without trusting producer counts states or digests
  + [LAS-026] verification reports exact stitches hints sources observations coordinates projections projected inclusions boundary-kind counts transition dispositions refusal counts maximum and total projected bytes evidence references and fourteen effect counters; all effects are zero
  + [LAS-027] unknown duplicate overbound profile identity source scope authority class lifecycle predecessor observation ordering predicate priority coordinate interval raw-byte digest count state disposition projection and fully redigested semantic mutations fail closed with typed faults and no partial output

& [AuthorityAndFixture]
  + [LAS-028] production exposes supplied-data parsing normalization hashing compilation lifecycle evaluation rendering and independent verification only and performs no filesystem environment clock process network provider model inference prompt mutation MCP Git workspace secret permission activation remote hardware or external action
  + [LAS-029] first retained fixture is synthetic provider-free with two stitches eight total hints four source bindings six observations four invocation coordinates five projected stitch inclusions two activations one fulfillment one invalidation zero refused transitions and zero effects; its values prove mechanics only
  + [LAS-030] hint optimality inference acceleration prompt placement live model behavior autonomous work host integration durable custody successor activation remote machines FPGA Minecraft and every physical effect remain separately sourced and signed

& [Acceptance]
